		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=32244#p32244"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>c&#039;est parce que ma base de donnée est sur un NAS.<br /># &quot;local&quot; is for Unix domain socket connections only<br />local&#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256<br /># IPv4 local connections:<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;postgres&#160; &#160; 127.0.0.1/32&#160; &#160; &#160;reject<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;127.0.0.1/32&#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256<br /># IPv6 local connections:<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; postgres&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;::1/128&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;reject<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;::1/128&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256</p><p>désolé de ne pas être très claire.<br />si j&#039;ai instauré une règle pour ipv6 je dois la mettre pour ipv4?</p>]]></content>
