		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  gestiin role postgres]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=32242#p32242"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>merci,<br />voici une config auquel j&#039;ai pensé</p><p># IPv4 local connections:<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;127.0.0.1/32&#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256<br /># IPv6 local connections:<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; postgres&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ::1/128&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;reject<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;::1/128&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256</p><p>l&#039;idée est de bloquer l&#039;utilisateur postgres uniquement sur une connexion distante.</p>]]></content>
